│   │   ├── users/
│   │   └── configuration/
│   └── _configs/
├── (website)/               # Public website
└── _common/                 # Shared components
    ├── components/
    ├── models/
    ├── utilities/
    └── services/
```

## Environment Variables

### Backend Required
```bash
DATABASE_URL=mongodb://localhost:27017/genedu
OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_key
GAMMA_API_KEY=your_gamma_key
JWT_SECRET=your_jwt_secret
```

## Key Features

### Media Processing
- YouTube video download using `@distube/ytdl-core`
- File upload with metadata extraction (size, duration)
- Audio conversion using FFmpeg
- Multiple audio chunk processing for large files

### AI Integration
- **OpenAI Whisper**: Audio transcription
- **OpenAI ChatGPT**: Educational text generation
- **Gamma API**: Professional presentation creation

### User Interface
- Responsive admin panel with dark/light mode
- Real-time status updates
- File preview with metadata
- Download functionality for generated content
- Toast notifications for user feedback

## Development Guidelines

### Code Style
- Use TypeScript strict mode
- Follow NestJS conventions for backend
- Use React Hook Form for form management
- Implement proper error handling with colored logs
- Use PrimeReact components for UI consistency

### Database Operations
- **NEVER** use `prisma db push` (dangerous for MongoDB)
- Use `yarn generate` to update Prisma client
- Use mongo-migrate-ts for schema migrations

### File Handling
- Store files in `uploads/medias/` directory
- Extract metadata (size, duration) for uploaded files
- Clean up old files when updating/deleting content
- Use proper file validation and error handling

### API Integration
- Implement proper error handling for external APIs
- Use colored logs for debugging
- Handle rate limits and timeouts
- Implement retry mechanisms where appropriate

## Common Patterns

### Service Methods
```typescript
// Standard processing method pattern
async processStep() {
  try {
    const pendings = await this.getPendings(limit)
    if (pendings?.length <= 0) return result
    
    const promises = pendings.map(content => this.processContent(content))
    const results = await Promise.all(promises)
    
    // Handle results and errors
    return result
  } catch (error) {
    coloredLog({ content: `Error: ${error.message}`, color: "red" })
    throw error
  }
}
```

### Frontend Form Pattern
```typescript
// Standard form with react-hook-form
const { control, handleSubmit, reset } = useForm<Model>()
const [formData, setFormData] = useState({ ...model })

async function save(params: Model) {
  const data = { /* map form data */ }
  const form = convertJsonToFormData(data)
  const saved = await Service.save(form, params.id)
  // Handle success/error
}
```

## Testing & Debugging

### Logs
- Use `coloredLog` utility for consistent logging
- Different colors for different log levels
- Include context information in log messages

### Error Handling
- Implement try-catch blocks in all async operations
- Provide meaningful error messages
- Update content status to ERROR on failures
- Store error details in `messageError` field

## Deployment Notes

### Production Setup
- Use PM2 for process management
- Configure MongoDB replica set
- Set up proper environment variables
- Use production build for frontend
- Configure file upload limits

### Monitoring
- Monitor bot service for continuous operation
- Track API usage and rate limits
- Monitor file storage usage
- Set up error alerting

